You were running down the night streets as fast as you could, and soon the many-storied buildings gave way to small private houses. You found a broken half-ruined shack and decided to wait there for dawn. You curled yourself up into a ball and fell asleep. The morning chill woke you up at the crack of dawn. You snuck into the neighboring courtyard and took a shirt and a pair of trousers off their clothesline. You quickly got dressed and headed towards the highway. You felt like yourself again, with the exception of feeling heavy remorse about the pathologist. But the most important question was what or who made you turn into a wolf. You was absolutely sure that no animal bit or even scratched you. You were confused. As ill luck would have it, there were no cars on the road when you badly needed to get home. Moreover, you were hungry again. You saw a bar for truck drivers behind the trees, and decided to go there.